// EXPECTED: compile error
// expect-error: read-modify-write
// BUG-803 (2026-08-17): a BIT-RANGE write is an IMPLICIT read-modify-write — the
// emitter lowers `flags[3..0] = 5` to
//     *p = (*p & ~(((1ull << 4) - 1) << 0)) | ((5 << 0) & mask)
// so an interrupt or a concurrent thread landing between the load and the store
// loses the update. Both RMW gates asked the wrong question: one tested whether
// the OPERATOR was compound, the other whether the RHS mentioned the global. A
// bit-range write is spelled `=` and its RHS (`5`) never names the global, so both
// disjuncts were false at BOTH sinks. The `+=` spelling of the identical operation
// was correctly rejected the whole time, which makes this the SPELLING axis of one
// question, not a new rule.
//
// Also fixed underneath: `resolve_write_target_global` peeled FIELD/INDEX/deref
// but not NODE_SLICE, so the walk returned NULL and the write was invisible to
// every caller of the shared resolver.
volatile u32 flags;
void bump() { flags[3..0] = 5; }
u32 main() { spawn bump(); flags[3..0] = 1; return 0; }
